Theorem TF-15a: SetTag transfer produces no dst (in-place tag mutation; row "—")

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `SetTag { base, tag }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-15a +
      Appendix A row 15
    - `SetTag` performs in-place tag mutation of `base`'s discriminant
      field; the `tag` operand is a scalar `u64` discriminant value
    - Appendix A row 15 carries "—" across every per-dimension column —
      no forward transfer (the instruction defines no SSA value)
    - Backward demand `(base, Once)` ONLY (no `value` operand — `tag` is
      a scalar u64 with no RC interaction) is proven at §04.3 TF-11
    - SetTag has NO IA-5 step (1) alias-transfer (no value operand;
      tag is a SCALAR-equivalent u64). Per Annex E §AIMS IA-5 step
      (1) clause (e): "SetTag: no value operand."

  Soundness property:
    Forall SetTag { base, tag }.
      transfer_tf15a(SetTag) = NoDst (no AimsState emitted)
    AND Appendix A row 15 carries "—" across every per-dimension column.
    Backward demand restricted to `(base, Once)` — no `value` operand.
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity holds trivially — no output state to
    monotone over.

  Proof obligation:
