      (a) No-dst confirmation — verify TF-15a emits NoDst (the "—"
          marker in Appendix A row 15). The state map MUST NOT acquire
          a new entry from this instruction.
      (b) Per-dimension "—" verification — every Appendix A row 15
          column reads "—" verbatim.
      (c) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — vacuously holds (same argument
          as TF-15 part (c)).

    Part (a) — no-dst confirmation:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-15a: "SetTag { base, tag }: in-place tag
      mutation. No `dst`. `tag` = scalar `u64`."
      Verified: transfer_tf15a() returns a NoDst marker (not Tagged::State,
      not Tagged::Scalar). The state map MUST be UNCHANGED by SetTag.
      Distinct from TF-15: SetTag has NO `value` operand to forward,
      hence no IA-5 step (1) alias-transfer on a value operand (the
      tag is a SCALAR-equivalent u64 with no RC interaction).

    Part (b) — Appendix A row "—" verification:
      Appendix A row 15 columns:
        Access: —; Consumption: —; Cardinality: —; Uniqueness: —;
        Locality: —; Shape: —; Effect: —.
      Verified: TF-15a enumeration emits no per-dimension column.

    Part (c) — vacuous monotonicity:
      Same vacuous argument as TF-15 part (c): the forward-transfer
      codomain is empty for no-dst instructions; L-6 layer (b)
      monotonicity holds trivially.
      Cross-reference: backward-demand monotonicity (TF-11 emits
      `(base, Once)` ONLY for SetTag — no value operand) is proven at
      §04.3 TF-11.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — vacuous L-6 layer (b) discharge for
        no-dst instructions per section_04::verify_tf15a_settag_no_dst)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 15 "—" enumeration per
        section_04::verify_tf15a_settag_no_dst)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; no codomain element)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-15a emits no dst,
        no refine() applicable)

